cookbook/references/kaggriculture-configs-follow-isaiahs-scaling-6m-recipe.md:17:- **`configs/kaggriculture_2rank.yaml`** (128 envs/rank, `segments_per_minibatch` 8, accumulation 1) **`configs/kaggriculture_4rank.yaml`** (64/4/1) and **`configs/kaggriculture_8rank.yaml`** (32/2/1, added 2026-09-29 for the owner's likely 8-rank main run; see the [[../decisions/start-multi-gpu-qualification-with-two-ranks|multi-GPU Decision]]). This is Isaiah's 6M multi-GPU division from `winner_ce_6m_4x5090.yaml` (his per-rank fit of the different `winner_ce_6m` recipe): divide `n_envs` and `segments_per_minibatch` by the world size and keep the global batch. His only 8-GPU config, `scaling_50m`, keeps 256 envs/rank instead, so it is not the precedent for a 6M global workload. Everything else is `scaling_6m`'s:
cookbook/references/kaggriculture-configs-follow-isaiahs-scaling-6m-recipe.md:31:- **Tests:** `tests/scripts/test_run_ppo.py` drives `run_ppo.main` from the shipped YAML through the real `FullConfig.from_file`; only the release-build check, torch setup and the distributed session are stubbed, and the run-dir, env and model steps are fail-if-reached sentinels. A `-o model.embed_dim=2097152 model.n_heads=65536` override fails the check with no headroom lines and no run directory. The 2-, 4- and 8-rank configs print the headroom lines and then stop with the explicit not-wired error, with no run directory. A real resume directory saved at 2 ranks and resumed on 1 checks the adapted 512 rollout rows. `tests/owl/train/test_config.py` again loads every `configs/*.yaml`, as in Isaiah's tree.
cookbook/references/kaggriculture-configs-follow-isaiahs-scaling-6m-recipe.md:33:| Workload (preset) | 2 ranks: rows, max trunk / exact head calls | 4 ranks | 8 ranks |
cookbook/references/kaggriculture-configs-follow-isaiahs-scaling-6m-recipe.md:51:- **8-rank addition (2026-09-29):** `_isaiah_per_rank_shape` in `tests/kaggriculture/test_configs.py` derives each ranked config's per-rank `n_envs`, `segments_per_minibatch` and teacher chunk from `scaling_6m` divided by the world size and raises when a global quantity, a per-rank minibatch or a teacher chunk does not divide whole (world sizes 3 and 32, accumulation 3 and a 24-segment teacher chunk are rejected). The 8-rank config passes the same global-workload, PPO-equality, headroom and `run_ppo.main` startup tests as the others; changing its spm to 4 failed four config tests. `py-prepare` for this change is recorded in the [[../decisions/start-multi-gpu-qualification-with-two-ranks|multi-GPU Decision]]'s log entry.
cookbook/references/kaggriculture-configs-follow-isaiahs-scaling-6m-recipe.md:61:- **Memory is unmeasured.** The spm 8 / accumulation 1 split holds only if the Task 6.1 memory smoke confirms it; otherwise the plan moves to 4 / 2 with the same product. The 8-rank shape (32 envs, spm 2) is qualified only by Task 6.3b on an owner-approved 8-GPU pod.
